sparky-stereo-headset (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The headset's battery in Plasma's own battery list (ORDER 108 milestone 14, ORDER 700): the new system service sparky-stereo-headset-battery and the udev rule 72-sparky-stereo-headset-battery.rules give UPower the charge that HeadsetControl reads, for the headsets the kernel has no driver for; the units start with the headset (SYSTEMD_WANTS in 71-sparky-stereo-headset.rules) and stop with it.
  * The low-battery notice that the user service sent is gone: PowerDevil tells the person once, at its own level for peripherals.
  * Ten languages: the two strings of the old notice are out of the catalogues.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:30:00 -0300

sparky-stereo-headset (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release (ORDER 696): the Headset page of System Settings, the panel entry and the user service, over HeadsetControl.

